"outputs/b3e3be9a-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Superdense coding {#superdense-coding}"
msgstr "Superdense coding {#superdense-coding}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Superdense coding is a protocol that, in some sense, achieves a complementary aim to teleportation.\n"
"Rather than allowing for the transmission of one qubit using two classical bits of communication (at the cost of one e-bit of entanglement), it allows for the transmission of two classical bits using one qubit of quantum communication (again, at the cost of one e-bit of entanglement).\n"
msgstr ""
"Superdense coding adalah protokol yang, dalam arti tertentu, mencapai tujuan yang komplementer dengan teleportasi.\n"
"Daripada memungkinkan transmisi satu qubit menggunakan dua bit komunikasi klasik (dengan biaya satu e-bit dari entanglement), ia memungkinkan transmisi dua bit klasik menggunakan satu qubit komunikasi kuantum (sekali lagi, dengan biaya satu e-bit dari entanglement).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In greater detail, we have a sender (Alice) and a receiver (Bob) that share one e-bit of entanglement.\n"
"According to the conventions in place for the lesson, this means that Alice holds a qubit $\\mathsf{A},$ Bob holds a qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ and together the pair $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ is in the state $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"
"Alice wishes to transmit two classical bits to Bob, which we'll denote by $c$ and $d,$ and she will accomplish this by sending him one qubit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lebih rincinya, kita punya pengirim (Alice) dan penerima (Bob) yang berbagi satu e-bit entanglement.\n"
"Sesuai konvensi yang berlaku untuk pelajaran ini, ini berarti Alice memegang qubit $\\mathsf{A},$ Bob memegang qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ dan bersama-sama pasangan $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ berada dalam keadaan $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"
"Alice ingin mengirimkan dua bit klasik ke Bob, yang akan kita sebut $c$ dan $d,$ dan dia akan melakukan ini dengan mengirimkan satu qubit kepadanya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is reasonable to view this feat as being less interesting than the one that teleportation accomplishes.\n"
"Sending qubits is likely to be so much more difficult than sending classical bits for the foreseeable future that trading one qubit of quantum communication for two bits of classical communication, at the cost of an e-bit no less, hardly seems worth it.\n"
"However, this does not imply that superdense coding is not interesting, for it most certainly is.\n"
msgstr ""
"Adalah wajar untuk memandang pencapaian ini sebagai kurang menarik dibanding yang dilakukan teleportasi.\n"
"Mengirimkan qubit kemungkinan akan jauh lebih sulit daripada mengirimkan bit klasik untuk waktu yang bisa kita perkirakan sehingga menukar satu qubit komunikasi kuantum dengan dua bit komunikasi klasik, dengan biaya satu e-bit pula, hampir tidak tampak sepadan.\n"
"Namun, ini tidak berarti bahwa superdense coding tidak menarik, karena tentu saja ia sangat menarik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Fitting the theme of the lesson, one reason why superdense coding is interesting is that it demonstrates a concrete and (in the context of information theory) rather striking use of entanglement.\n"
"A famous theorem in quantum information theory, known as *Holevo's theorem*, implies that without the use of a shared entangled state, it is impossible to communicate more than one bit of classical information by sending a single qubit.\n"
"(Holevo's theorem is more general than this.\n"
"Its precise statement is technical and requires explanation, but this is one consequence of it.)\n"
"So, through superdense coding, shared entanglement effectively allows for the *doubling* of the classical information-carrying capacity of sending qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sesuai tema pelajaran ini, salah satu alasan mengapa superdense coding menarik adalah bahwa ia mendemonstrasikan penggunaan entanglement yang konkret dan (dalam konteks teori informasi) cukup mencolok.\n"
"Sebuah teorema terkenal dalam teori informasi kuantum, yang dikenal sebagai *Teorema Holevo*, menyiratkan bahwa tanpa menggunakan keadaan terbelit bersama, adalah mustahil untuk mengkomunikasikan lebih dari satu bit informasi klasik dengan mengirimkan satu qubit.\n"
"(Teorema Holevo lebih umum dari ini.\n"
"Pernyataan pastinya bersifat teknis dan memerlukan penjelasan, tetapi ini adalah salah satu konsekuensinya.)\n"
"Jadi, melalui superdense coding, entanglement bersama secara efektif memungkinkan *penggandaan* kapasitas pembawa informasi klasik dari pengiriman qubit.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Protocol {#protocol}"
msgstr "Protokol {#protocol}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following quantum circuit diagram describes the superdense coding "
"protocol:\n"
msgstr ""
"Diagram Circuit kuantum berikut menggambarkan protokol superdense coding:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Superdense coding circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/superdense-"
"coding.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Superdense coding circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/superdense-"
"coding.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In words, here is what Alice does:\n"
msgstr "Dalam kata-kata, inilah yang Alice lakukan:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $d=1,$ Alice performs a $Z$ gate on her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ (and if $d=0$"
" she does not).\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika $d=1,$ Alice melakukan Gate $Z$ pada Qubitnya $\\mathsf{A}$ (dan jika "
"$d=0$ dia tidak melakukannya).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $c=1,$ Alice performs an $X$ gate on her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ (and if "
"$c=0$ she does not).\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika $c=1,$ Alice melakukan Gate $X$ pada Qubitnya $\\mathsf{A}$ (dan jika "
"$c=0$ dia tidak melakukannya).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alice then sends her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ to Bob.\n"
msgstr "Alice kemudian mengirimkan Qubitnya $\\mathsf{A}$ kepada Bob.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What Bob does when he receives the qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ is to first perform a controlled-NOT gate, with $\\mathsf{A}$ being the control and $\\mathsf{B}$ being the target, and then he applies a Hadamard gate to $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
"He then measures $\\mathsf{B}$ to obtain $c$ and $\\mathsf{A}$ to obtain $d,$ with standard basis measurements in both cases.\n"
msgstr ""
"Yang Bob lakukan ketika menerima qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ adalah pertama-tama melakukan Gate controlled-NOT, dengan $\\mathsf{A}$ sebagai kontrol dan $\\mathsf{B}$ sebagai target, dan kemudian dia menerapkan Gate Hadamard ke $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
"Dia kemudian mengukur $\\mathsf{B}$ untuk mendapatkan $c$ dan $\\mathsf{A}$ untuk mendapatkan $d,$ dengan pengukuran basis standar di kedua kasus.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Analysis {#analysis}"
msgstr "Analisis {#analysis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The idea behind this protocol is simple:\n"
"Alice effectively chooses which Bell state she would like to be sharing with Bob,\n"
"she sends Bob her qubit, and Bob measures to determine which Bell state Alice chose.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ide di balik protokol ini sederhana:\n"
"Alice secara efektif memilih keadaan Bell mana yang ingin dia bagikan dengan Bob,\n"
"dia mengirimkan Qubitnya kepada Bob, dan Bob mengukur untuk menentukan keadaan Bell mana yang Alice pilih.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, they initially share $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle,$ and depending upon the bits $c$ and $d,$ Alice either leaves this state alone or shifts it to one of the other Bell states by applying $\\mathbb{I},$ $X,$ $Z,$ or $XZ$ to her qubit\n"
"$\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Artinya, awalnya mereka berbagi $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle,$ dan tergantung pada bit $c$ dan $d,$ Alice baik membiarkan keadaan ini apa adanya atau menggesernya ke salah satu keadaan Bell lainnya dengan menerapkan $\\mathbb{I},$ $X,$ $Z,$ atau $XZ$ pada Qubitnya\n"
"$\\mathsf{A}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes X) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes XZ) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^-\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes X) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes XZ) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^-\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bob's actions have the following effects on the four Bell states:\n"
msgstr "Aksi Bob memiliki efek berikut pada keempat keadaan Bell:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 00\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 01\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 10\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto -\\vert 11\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 00\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 01\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 10\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto -\\vert 11\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This can be checked directly, by computing the results of Bob's operations "
"on these states one at a time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini bisa diperiksa secara langsung, dengan menghitung hasil operasi Bob pada"
" keadaan-keadaan ini satu per satu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, when Bob performs his measurements, he is able to determine which Bell state Alice chose.\n"
"To verify that the protocol works correctly is a matter of checking each case:\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, ketika Bob melakukan pengukurannya, dia dapat menentukan keadaan Bell mana yang Alice pilih.\n"
"Untuk memverifikasi bahwa protokol bekerja dengan benar adalah masalah memeriksa setiap kasus:\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $cd = 00,$ then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob "
"receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle.$ He transforms this state"
" into $\\vert 00\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 00.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika $cd = 00,$ maka keadaan $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ saat Bob menerima "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ adalah $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle.$ Dia mengubah keadaan ini "
"menjadi $\\vert 00\\rangle$ dan memperoleh $cd = 00.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $cd = 01,$ then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob "
"receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle.$ He transforms this state"
" into $\\vert 01\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 01.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika $cd = 01,$ maka keadaan $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ saat Bob menerima "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ adalah $\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle.$ Dia mengubah keadaan ini "
"menjadi $\\vert 01\\rangle$ dan memperoleh $cd = 01.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $cd = 10,$ then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob "
"receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle.$ He transforms this state"
" into $\\vert 10\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 10.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika $cd = 10,$ maka keadaan $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ saat Bob menerima "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ adalah $\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle.$ Dia mengubah keadaan ini "
"menjadi $\\vert 10\\rangle$ dan memperoleh $cd = 10.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $cd = 11,$ then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob "
"receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle.$ He transforms this state"
" into $-\\vert 11\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 11.$ (The negative-one phase "
"factor has no effect here.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika $cd = 11,$ maka keadaan $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ saat Bob menerima "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ adalah $\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle.$ Dia mengubah keadaan ini "
"menjadi $-\\vert 11\\rangle$ dan memperoleh $cd = 11.$ (Faktor fase negatif-"
"satu tidak berpengaruh di sini.)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Superdense coding implementation {#superdense-coding-implementation}"
msgstr "Implementasi superdense coding {#superdense-coding-implementation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here is a simple implementation of superdense coding where we specify the "
"circuit itself depending on the bits to be transmitted. First we'll choose "
"two bits to be transmitted. (Later we'll choose them randomly, but for now "
"we'll just make an arbitrary choice.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut ini adalah implementasi sederhana dari superdense coding di mana "
"kita menentukan Circuit itu sendiri tergantung pada bit yang akan dikirim. "
"Pertama kita akan memilih dua bit yang akan dikirim. (Nanti kita akan "
"memilihnya secara acak, tapi untuk sekarang kita hanya membuat pilihan "
"sembarang.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we'll build the circuit accordingly. Here we'll allow Qiskit to use the "
"default names for the qubits: $\\mathsf{q}_0$ for the top qubit and "
"$\\mathsf{q}_1$ for the bottom one.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita akan membangun Circuit sesuai dengan itu. Di sini kita akan "
"membiarkan Qiskit menggunakan nama default untuk qubit: $\\mathsf{q}_0$ "
"untuk qubit atas dan $\\mathsf{q}_1$ untuk yang bawah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/extracted-"
"outputs/05ae9b94-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
