#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The CHSH game {#the-chsh-game}"
msgstr "The CHSH game {#the-chsh-game}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The last example to be discussed in this lesson is not a protocol, but a *game* known as the\n"
"*CHSH game*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Contoh terakhir yang akan dibahas dalam pelajaran ini bukan sebuah protokol,"
" melainkan sebuah *permainan* yang dikenal sebagai *permainan CHSH*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When we speak of a game in this context, we're not talking about something that's meant to be played for fun or sport, but rather a mathematical abstraction in the sense of *game theory*.\n"
"Mathematical abstractions of games are studied in economics and computer science, for instance, and they are both fascinating and useful.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ketika kita berbicara tentang permainan dalam konteks ini, kita tidak sedang membicarakan sesuatu yang dimainkan untuk bersenang-senang atau olahraga, melainkan sebuah abstraksi matematis dalam pengertian *teori permainan*.\n"
"Abstraksi matematis dari permainan dipelajari dalam ilmu ekonomi dan ilmu komputer, misalnya, dan keduanya sangat menarik sekaligus berguna.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The letters CHSH refer to the authors — John Clauser, Michael Horne, Abner Shimony, and Richard Holt — of a 1969 paper where the example was first described.\n"
"They did not describe the example as a game, but rather as an experiment.\n"
"Its description as a game, however, is both natural and intuitive.\n"
msgstr ""
"Huruf CHSH merujuk pada para penulisnya — John Clauser, Michael Horne, Abner Shimony, dan Richard Holt — dari sebuah makalah tahun 1969 di mana contoh ini pertama kali dijelaskan.\n"
"Mereka tidak menggambarkan contoh ini sebagai permainan, melainkan sebagai eksperimen.\n"
"Namun deskripsinya sebagai permainan bersifat alami dan intuitif.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The CHSH game falls within a class of games known as *nonlocal games*.\n"
"Nonlocal games are incredibly interesting and have deep connections to physics, computer science, and mathematics — holding mysteries that still remain unsolved.\n"
"We'll begin the section by explaining what nonlocal games are, and then we'll focus in on the CHSH game and what makes it interesting.\n"
msgstr ""
"Permainan CHSH termasuk dalam kelas permainan yang dikenal sebagai *permainan nonlokal*.\n"
"Permainan nonlokal sangat menarik dan memiliki hubungan mendalam dengan fisika, ilmu komputer, dan matematika — menyimpan misteri yang hingga kini masih belum terpecahkan.\n"
"Kita akan mulai bagian ini dengan menjelaskan apa itu permainan nonlokal, kemudian akan fokus pada permainan CHSH dan apa yang membuatnya menarik.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Nonlocal games {#nonlocal-games}"
msgstr "Permainan nonlokal {#nonlocal-games}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A nonlocal game is a *cooperative game* where two players, Alice and Bob, work together to achieve a particular outcome.\n"
"The game is run by a *referee*, who behaves according to strict guidelines that are known to Alice and Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Permainan nonlokal adalah *permainan kooperatif* di mana dua pemain, Alice dan Bob, bekerja sama untuk mencapai hasil tertentu.\n"
"Permainan ini dijalankan oleh seorang *wasit*, yang bertindak sesuai pedoman ketat yang diketahui oleh Alice dan Bob.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice and Bob can prepare for the game however they choose, but once the game starts they are *forbidden from communicating*.\n"
"We might imagine the game taking place in a secure facility of some sort — as if the referee is playing the role of a detective and Alice and Bob are suspects being interrogated in different rooms.\n"
"But another way to think about the set-up is that Alice and Bob are separated by a vast distance, and communication is prohibited because the speed of light doesn't allow for it within the running time of the game.\n"
"That is to say, if Alice tries to send a message to Bob, the game will be over by the time he receives it, and vice versa.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice dan Bob bisa mempersiapkan diri sesuka mereka, tetapi setelah permainan dimulai mereka *dilarang berkomunikasi*.\n"
"Kita bisa membayangkan permainan ini berlangsung di sebuah fasilitas keamanan — seolah wasit berperan sebagai detektif dan Alice serta Bob adalah tersangka yang diinterogasi di ruangan berbeda.\n"
"Tapi cara lain untuk memikirkan situasinya adalah bahwa Alice dan Bob terpisah oleh jarak yang sangat jauh, dan komunikasi dilarang karena kecepatan cahaya tidak memungkinkan dalam waktu berjalannya permainan.\n"
"Artinya, jika Alice mencoba mengirim pesan ke Bob, permainan sudah selesai sebelum dia menerimanya, begitu pula sebaliknya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The way a nonlocal game works is that the referee first asks Alice and Bob one question each.\n"
"We'll use the letter $x$ to refer to Alice's question and $y$ to refer to Bob's question.\n"
"Here we're thinking of $x$ and $y$ as being classical states, and in the CHSH game $x$ and $y$ are bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cara kerja permainan nonlokal adalah wasit pertama-tama mengajukan satu pertanyaan masing-masing kepada Alice dan Bob.\n"
"Kita akan menggunakan huruf $x$ untuk merujuk pada pertanyaan Alice dan $y$ untuk pertanyaan Bob.\n"
"Di sini kita menganggap $x$ dan $y$ sebagai keadaan klasik, dan dalam permainan CHSH $x$ dan $y$ adalah bit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The referee uses *randomness* to select these questions.\n"
"To be precise, there is some probability $p(x,y)$ associated with each possible pair $(x,y)$ of questions, and the referee has vowed to choose the questions randomly, at the time of the game, in this way.\n"
"Everyone, including Alice and Bob, knows these probabilities — but nobody knows specifically which pair $(x,y)$ will be chosen until the game begins.\n"
msgstr ""
"Wasit menggunakan *keacakan* untuk memilih pertanyaan-pertanyaan ini.\n"
"Lebih tepatnya, ada probabilitas $p(x,y)$ yang terkait dengan setiap pasangan pertanyaan $(x,y)$ yang mungkin, dan wasit telah berjanji untuk memilih pertanyaan secara acak, pada saat permainan berlangsung, dengan cara ini.\n"
"Semua orang, termasuk Alice dan Bob, mengetahui probabilitas-probabilitas ini — tetapi tidak ada yang tahu secara spesifik pasangan $(x,y)$ mana yang akan dipilih sampai permainan dimulai.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After Alice and Bob receive their questions, they must then provide answers: Alice's answer is $a$ and Bob's answer is $b.$\n"
"Again, these are classical states in general, and bits in the CHSH game.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah Alice dan Bob menerima pertanyaan mereka, mereka harus memberikan jawaban: jawaban Alice adalah $a$ dan jawaban Bob adalah $b.$\n"
"Sekali lagi, ini adalah keadaan klasik secara umum, dan bit dalam permainan CHSH.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point the referee makes a decision: Alice and Bob either *win* or *lose* depending on whether or not the pair of answers $(a,b)$ is deemed correct for the pair of questions $(x,y)$ according to some fixed set of rules.\n"
"Different rules mean different games, and the rules for the CHSH game specifically are described in the section following this one.\n"
"As was already suggested, the rules are known to everyone.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada titik ini wasit membuat keputusan: Alice dan Bob menang atau kalah tergantung apakah pasangan jawaban $(a,b)$ dianggap benar untuk pasangan pertanyaan $(x,y)$ sesuai dengan seperangkat aturan yang telah ditetapkan.\n"
"Aturan yang berbeda berarti permainan yang berbeda, dan aturan untuk permainan CHSH secara khusus dijelaskan pada bagian berikutnya.\n"
"Seperti yang sudah disebutkan, aturan diketahui oleh semua orang.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following diagram provides a graphic representation of the "
"interactions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Diagram berikut memberikan representasi grafis dari interaksi tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Nonlocal game](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/nonlocal-"
"game.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Nonlocal game](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/nonlocal-"
"game.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is the uncertainty about which questions will be asked, and specifically "
"the fact that each player doesn't know the other player's question, that "
"makes nonlocal games challenging for Alice and Bob — just like colluding "
"suspects in different rooms trying to keep their story straight.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ketidakpastian tentang pertanyaan mana yang akan diajukan, dan khususnya "
"fakta bahwa setiap pemain tidak mengetahui pertanyaan pemain lain, membuat "
"permainan nonlokal menjadi tantangan bagi Alice dan Bob — sama seperti "
"tersangka yang berkolusi di ruangan berbeda yang mencoba menjaga cerita "
"mereka tetap konsisten.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A precise description of the referee defines an instance of a nonlocal game.\n"
"This includes a specification of the probabilities $p(x,y)$ for each question pair along with the rules\n"
"that determine whether each pair of answers $(a,b)$ wins or loses for each possible question pair $(x,y).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Deskripsi yang tepat tentang wasit mendefinisikan sebuah instansi permainan nonlokal.\n"
"Ini mencakup spesifikasi probabilitas $p(x,y)$ untuk setiap pasangan pertanyaan beserta aturan yang menentukan apakah setiap pasangan jawaban $(a,b)$ menang atau kalah untuk setiap pasangan pertanyaan $(x,y)$ yang mungkin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll take a look at the CHSH game momentarily, but before that let us briefly acknowledge that it's also interesting to consider other nonlocal games.\n"
"In fact, it's extremely interesting; there are some pretty simple nonlocal games for which it's currently not known how well Alice and Bob can play using entanglement.\n"
"The set-up is simple, but there's complexity at work — and for some games it can be impossibly difficult to compute best or near-best strategies for Alice and Bob.\n"
"This is the surprisingly unintuitive nature of the nonlocal games model.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan melihat permainan CHSH sebentar lagi, tetapi sebelum itu mari kita akui secara singkat bahwa sangat menarik untuk mempertimbangkan permainan nonlokal lainnya.\n"
"Faktanya, ini sangat menarik; ada beberapa permainan nonlokal yang cukup sederhana di mana saat ini belum diketahui seberapa baik Alice dan Bob bisa bermain menggunakan keterikatan.\n"
"Pengaturannya sederhana, tetapi ada kompleksitas yang bekerja — dan untuk beberapa permainan bisa sangat sulit untuk menghitung strategi terbaik atau mendekati terbaik bagi Alice dan Bob.\n"
"Inilah sifat yang mengejutkan dan tidak intuitif dari model permainan nonlokal.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "CHSH game description {#chsh-game-description}"
msgstr "Deskripsi permainan CHSH {#chsh-game-description}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here is the precise description of the CHSH game, where (as above) $x$ is "
"Alice's question, $y$ is Bob's question, $a$ is Alice's answer, and $b$ is "
"Bob's answer:\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah deskripsi tepat dari permainan CHSH, di mana (seperti di "
"atas) $x$ adalah pertanyaan Alice, $y$ adalah pertanyaan Bob, $a$ adalah "
"jawaban Alice, dan $b$ adalah jawaban Bob:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The questions and answers are all bits: $x,y,a,b\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"
msgstr "Pertanyaan dan jawabannya semuanya adalah bit: $x,y,a,b\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The referee chooses the questions $(x,y)$ *uniformly at random*. That is, "
"each of the four possibilities, $(0,0),$ $(0,1),$ $(1,0),$ and $(1,1),$ is "
"selected with probability $1/4.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Wasit memilih pertanyaan $(x,y)$ *secara seragam secara acak*. Artinya, "
"masing-masing dari empat kemungkinan, $(0,0),$ $(0,1),$ $(1,0),$ dan "
"$(1,1),$ dipilih dengan probabilitas $1/4.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The answers $(a,b)$ *win* for the questions $(x,y)$ if $a\\oplus b = "
"x\\wedge y$ and *lose* otherwise. The following table expresses this rule by"
" listing the winning and losing conditions on the answers $(a,b)$ for each "
"pair of questions $(x,y).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Jawaban $(a,b)$ *menang* untuk pertanyaan $(x,y)$ jika $a\\oplus b = "
"x\\wedge y$ dan *kalah* sebaliknya. Tabel berikut mengungkapkan aturan ini "
"dengan mencantumkan kondisi menang dan kalah pada jawaban $(a,b)$ untuk "
"setiap pasangan pertanyaan $(x,y).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccc}\n"
"(x,y) & \\text{win} & \\text{lose} \\\\[1mm]\\hline\n"
"\\rule{0mm}{4mm}(0,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(0,1) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,1) & a \\neq b & a = b\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccc}\n"
"(x,y) & \\text{win} & \\text{lose} \\\\[1mm]\\hline\n"
"\\rule{0mm}{4mm}(0,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(0,1) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,1) & a \\neq b & a = b\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Limitation of classical strategies {#limitation-of-classical-strategies}"
msgstr "Keterbatasan strategi klasik {#limitation-of-classical-strategies}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's consider strategies for Alice and Bob in the CHSH game, beginning "
"with *classical* strategies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang mari kita pertimbangkan strategi untuk Alice dan Bob dalam "
"permainan CHSH, dimulai dengan strategi *klasik*.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Deterministic strategies {#deterministic-strategies}"
msgstr "Strategi deterministik {#deterministic-strategies}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll start with *deterministic* strategies, where Alice's answer $a$ is a function of the question $x$ that she receives, and likewise Bob's answer $b$ is a function of the question $y$ he receives.\n"
"So, for instance, we may write $a(0)$ to represent Alice's answer when her question is $0,$ and $a(1)$ to represent Alice's answer when her question is $1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan mulai dengan strategi *deterministik*, di mana jawaban Alice $a$ adalah fungsi dari pertanyaan $x$ yang diterimanya, dan begitu pula jawaban Bob $b$ adalah fungsi dari pertanyaan $y$ yang diterimanya.\n"
"Jadi, misalnya, kita bisa menulis $a(0)$ untuk mewakili jawaban Alice ketika pertanyaannya adalah $0,$ dan $a(1)$ untuk mewakili jawaban Alice ketika pertanyaannya adalah $1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"No deterministic strategy can possibly win the CHSH game every time.\n"
"One way to understand this is simply to go one-by-one through all of the possible deterministic strategies and check that every one of them loses for at least one of the four possible question pairs.\n"
"Alice and Bob can each choose from four possible functions from one bit to one bit — which we encountered in the lesson on [Single systems](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/introduction) — and so there are $16$ different deterministic strategies in total to check.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tidak ada strategi deterministik yang bisa memenangkan permainan CHSH setiap saat.\n"
"Salah satu cara untuk memahami ini adalah dengan memeriksa satu per satu semua strategi deterministik yang mungkin dan memverifikasi bahwa setiap strategi kalah untuk setidaknya satu dari empat pasangan pertanyaan yang mungkin.\n"
"Alice dan Bob masing-masing bisa memilih dari empat fungsi yang mungkin dari satu bit ke satu bit — yang kita temui dalam pelajaran tentang [Single systems](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/introduction) — sehingga ada $16$ strategi deterministik yang berbeda untuk diperiksa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also reason this analytically.\n"
"If Alice and Bob's strategy wins when $(x,y) = (0,0),$ then it must be that $a(0) = b(0);$\n"
"if their strategy wins when $(x,y) = (0,1),$ then $a(0) = b(1);$ and similarly,\n"
"if the strategy wins for $(x,y)=(1,0)$ then $a(1) = b(0).$\n"
"So, if their strategy wins for all three possibilities, then\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita juga bisa mereasonkan ini secara analitik.\n"
"Jika strategi Alice dan Bob menang ketika $(x,y) = (0,0),$ maka harus ada $a(0) = b(0);$\n"
"jika strategi mereka menang ketika $(x,y) = (0,1),$ maka $a(0) = b(1);$ dan serupa,\n"
"jika strategi menang untuk $(x,y)=(1,0)$ maka $a(1) = b(0).$\n"
"Jadi, jika strategi mereka menang untuk ketiga kemungkinan tersebut, maka\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"b(1) = a(0) = b(0) = a(1).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"b(1) = a(0) = b(0) = a(1).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies that the strategy loses in the final case $(x,y) = (1,1),$ and for here winning requires that\n"
"$a(1) \\neq b(1).$\n"
"Thus, there can be no deterministic strategy that wins every time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini berarti strategi tersebut kalah dalam kasus terakhir $(x,y) = (1,1),$ dan di sini menang membutuhkan bahwa\n"
"$a(1) \\neq b(1).$\n"
"Jadi, tidak ada strategi deterministik yang bisa menang setiap saat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the other hand, it is easy to find deterministic strategies that win in three of the four cases, such as $a(0)=a(1)=b(0)=b(1)=0.$\n"
"From this we conclude that the maximum probability for Alice and Bob to win using a deterministic strategy is $3/4.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sisi lain, mudah untuk menemukan strategi deterministik yang menang dalam tiga dari empat kasus, seperti $a(0)=a(1)=b(0)=b(1)=0.$\n"
"Dari sini kita menyimpulkan bahwa probabilitas maksimum bagi Alice dan Bob untuk menang menggunakan strategi deterministik adalah $3/4.$\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic strategies {#probabilistic-strategies}"
msgstr "Strategi probabilistik {#probabilistic-strategies}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As we just concluded, Alice and Bob cannot do better than winning the CHSH game 75% of the time using a deterministic strategy.\n"
"But what about a probabilistic strategy?\n"
"Could it help Alice and Bob to use randomness — including the possibility of *shared randomness*, where their random choices are correlated?\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti yang baru saja kita simpulkan, Alice dan Bob tidak bisa lebih baik dari memenangkan permainan CHSH 75% dari waktu menggunakan strategi deterministik.\n"
"Tapi bagaimana dengan strategi probabilistik?\n"
"Apakah bisa membantu Alice dan Bob menggunakan keacakan — termasuk kemungkinan *keacakan bersama*, di mana pilihan acak mereka berkorelasi?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It turns out that probabilistic strategies don't help at all to increase the probability that Alice and Bob win.\n"
"This is because every probabilistic strategy can alternatively be viewed as a random selection of a deterministic strategy, just like (as was mentioned in the [Single systems](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/introduction) lesson) probabilistic operations can be viewed as random selections of deterministic operations.\n"
"The average is never larger than the maximum, and so it follows that probabilistic strategies don't offer any advantage in terms of their overall winning probability.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ternyata strategi probabilistik sama sekali tidak membantu untuk meningkatkan probabilitas Alice dan Bob menang.\n"
"Ini karena setiap strategi probabilistik dapat secara alternatif dipandang sebagai pemilihan acak dari strategi deterministik, seperti halnya (seperti yang disebutkan dalam pelajaran [Single systems](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/introduction)) operasi probabilistik dapat dipandang sebagai pemilihan acak dari operasi deterministik.\n"
"Rata-rata tidak pernah lebih besar dari maksimum, sehingga strategi probabilistik tidak menawarkan keuntungan apa pun dalam hal probabilitas menang secara keseluruhan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thus, winning with probability $3/4$ is the best that Alice and Bob can do "
"using any classical strategy, whether deterministic or probabilistic.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, menang dengan probabilitas $3/4$ adalah yang terbaik yang bisa "
"dilakukan Alice dan Bob menggunakan strategi klasik apa pun, baik "
"deterministik maupun probabilistik.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "CHSH game strategy {#chsh-game-strategy}"
msgstr "Strategi permainan CHSH {#chsh-game-strategy}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A natural question to ask at this point is whether Alice and Bob can do any better using a *quantum* strategy.\n"
"In particular, if they share an entangled quantum state as the following figure suggests, which they could have prepared prior to playing the game, can they increase their winning probability?\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertanyaan alami yang perlu ditanyakan saat ini adalah apakah Alice dan Bob bisa berbuat lebih baik menggunakan strategi *kuantum*.\n"
"Secara khusus, jika mereka berbagi keadaan kuantum yang terikat seperti yang disarankan gambar berikut, yang bisa mereka persiapkan sebelum memainkan permainan, apakah mereka bisa meningkatkan probabilitas menang mereka?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Nonlocal game with entanglement](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/nonlocal-"
"game-entanglement.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Nonlocal game with entanglement](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/nonlocal-"
"game-entanglement.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The answer is yes, and this is the main point of the example and why it's so interesting.\n"
"So let's see exactly how Alice and Bob can do better in this game using entanglement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jawabannya adalah ya, dan inilah poin utama dari contoh ini dan mengapa ini begitu menarik.\n"
"Jadi mari kita lihat secara tepat bagaimana Alice dan Bob bisa berbuat lebih baik dalam permainan ini menggunakan keterikatan.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Required vectors and matrices {#required-vectors-and-matrices}"
msgstr "Vektor dan matriks yang diperlukan {#required-vectors-and-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first thing we need to do is to define a qubit state vector $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle,$ for each real number\n"
"$\\theta$ (which we'll think of as an angle measured in radians) as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hal pertama yang perlu kita lakukan adalah mendefinisikan vektor keadaan qubit $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle,$ untuk setiap bilangan real\n"
"$\\theta$ (yang akan kita anggap sebagai sudut yang diukur dalam radian) sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here are some simple examples:\n"
msgstr "Berikut beberapa contoh sederhana:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{0}\\rangle & = \\vert 0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/2}\\rangle & = \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert + \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{0}\\rangle & = \\vert 0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/2}\\rangle & = \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert + \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We also have the following examples, which arise in the analysis below:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita juga memiliki contoh-contoh berikut, yang muncul dalam analisis di "
"bawah ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Looking at the general form, we see that the inner product between any two "
"of these vectors has this formula:\n"
msgstr ""
"Melihat bentuk umumnya, kita melihat bahwa hasil kali dalam antara dua "
"vektor ini memiliki rumus berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha-\\beta).\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha-\\beta).\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In detail, there are only real number entries in these vectors, so there are no complex conjugates to worry about:\n"
"the inner product is the product of the cosines plus the product of the sines.\n"
"Using one of the *angle addition formulas* from trigonometry leads to the simplification above.\n"
"This formula reveals the geometric interpretation of the inner product between real unit vectors as the cosine of the angle between them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara rinci, hanya ada entri bilangan real dalam vektor-vektor ini, sehingga tidak ada konjugat kompleks yang perlu dikhawatirkan:\n"
"hasil kali dalam adalah hasil kali dari cosinus-cosinus ditambah hasil kali dari sinus-sinus.\n"
"Menggunakan salah satu *rumus penambahan sudut* dari trigonometri menghasilkan penyederhanaan di atas.\n"
"Rumus ini mengungkapkan interpretasi geometris dari hasil kali dalam antara vektor satuan real sebagai cosinus dari sudut di antara keduanya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we compute the inner product of the *tensor product* of any two of these "
"vectors with the $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$ state, we obtain a similar "
"expression, except that it has a $\\sqrt{2}$ in the denominator:\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika kita menghitung hasil kali dalam dari *hasil kali tensor* dari dua "
"vektor ini dengan keadaan $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle,$ kita mendapatkan "
"ekspresi serupa, kecuali bahwa ada $\\sqrt{2}$ di penyebutnya:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha-\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"\\tag{4}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha-\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"\\tag{4}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Our interest in this particular inner product will become clear shortly, but"
" for now we're simply observing this as a formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ketertarikan kita pada hasil kali dalam khusus ini akan menjadi jelas "
"segera, tetapi untuk saat ini kita hanya mengamati ini sebagai sebuah "
"rumus.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, define a unitary matrix $U_{\\theta}$ for each angle $\\theta$ as "
"follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya, definisikan matriks uniter $U_{\\theta}$ untuk setiap sudut "
"$\\theta$ sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta} = \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta} = \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Intuitively speaking, this matrix transforms $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ into $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ into $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"To check that this is a unitary matrix, a key observation is that the vectors $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ are orthogonal for every angle $\\theta$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara intuitif, matriks ini mengubah $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ menjadi $\\vert 0\\rangle$ dan $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ menjadi $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"Untuk memeriksa bahwa ini adalah matriks uniter, pengamatan kunci adalah bahwa vektor $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ dan $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ ortogonal untuk setiap sudut $\\theta$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2} \\rangle = \\cos(\\pi/2) = 0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2} \\rangle = \\cos(\\pi/2) = 0.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, we find that\n"
msgstr "Dengan demikian, kita menemukan bahwa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U_{\\theta} U_{\\theta}^{\\dagger}\n"
"& = \\bigl(\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2}\\rangle\\langle 1 \\vert\\bigr) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U_{\\theta} U_{\\theta}^{\\dagger}\n"
"& = \\bigl(\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2}\\rangle\\langle 1 \\vert\\bigr) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We may alternatively write this matrix explicitly as\n"
msgstr "Kita juga bisa menulis matriks ini secara eksplisit sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\theta+ \\pi/2) & \\sin(\\theta + \\pi/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"-\\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\theta+ \\pi/2) & \\sin(\\theta + \\pi/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"-\\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is an example of a *rotation matrix*, and specifically it rotates two-dimensional vectors with real number entries by an angle of $-\\theta$ about the origin.\n"
"If we follow a standard convention for naming and parameterizing rotations of various forms, we have\n"
"$U_{\\theta} = R_y(-2\\theta)$ where\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah contoh dari *matriks rotasi*, dan secara khusus memutar vektor dua dimensi dengan entri bilangan real sebesar sudut $-\\theta$ terhadap titik asal.\n"
"Jika kita mengikuti konvensi standar untuk penamaan dan parameterisasi rotasi dari berbagai bentuk, kita memiliki\n"
"$U_{\\theta} = R_y(-2\\theta)$ di mana\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta/2) & -\\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(\\theta/2) & \\cos(\\theta/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta/2) & -\\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(\\theta/2) & \\cos(\\theta/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Strategy description {#strategy-description}"
msgstr "Deskripsi strategi {#strategy-description}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now we can describe the quantum strategy.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita bisa mendeskripsikan strategi kuantum.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Set-up:** Alice and Bob start the game sharing an e-bit: Alice holds a "
"qubit $\\mathsf{A},$ Bob holds a qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ and together the two "
"qubits $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ are in the $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ "
"state.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Persiapan:** Alice dan Bob memulai permainan dengan berbagi e-bit: Alice "
"memegang qubit $\\mathsf{A},$ Bob memegang qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ dan bersama-"
"sama dua qubit $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ berada dalam keadaan "
"$\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Alice's actions:**\n"
msgstr "**Tindakan Alice:**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Alice receives the question $x=0,$ she applies $U_{0}$ to her qubit "
"$\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika Alice menerima pertanyaan $x=0,$ dia menerapkan $U_{0}$ pada Qubitnya "
"$\\mathsf{A}.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Alice receives the question  $x=1,$ she applies $U_{\\pi/4}$ to her qubit"
" $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika Alice menerima pertanyaan $x=1,$ dia menerapkan $U_{\\pi/4}$ pada "
"Qubitnya $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The operation Alice performs on $\\mathsf{A}$ may alternatively be described like this:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_0 & \\text{if $x = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{\\pi/4} & \\text{if $x = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  Operasi yang Alice lakukan pada $\\mathsf{A}$ bisa juga dideskripsikan seperti ini:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_0 & \\text{if $x = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{\\pi/4} & \\text{if $x = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  After Alice applies this operation, she measures $\\mathsf{A}$ with a "
"standard basis measurement and sets her answer $a$ to be the measurement "
"outcome.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Setelah Alice menerapkan operasi ini, dia mengukur $\\mathsf{A}$ dengan "
"pengukuran basis standar dan menetapkan jawabannya $a$ sebagai hasil "
"pengukuran.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Bob's actions:**\n"
msgstr "**Tindakan Bob:**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Bob receives the question $y=0,$ he applies $U_{\\pi/8}$ to his qubit "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika Bob menerima pertanyaan $y=0,$ dia menerapkan $U_{\\pi/8}$ pada "
"Qubitnya $\\mathsf{B}.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Bob receives the question $y=1,$ he applies $U_{-\\pi/8}$ to his qubit "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika Bob menerima pertanyaan $y=1,$ dia menerapkan $U_{-\\pi/8}$ pada "
"Qubitnya $\\mathsf{B}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Like we did for Alice, we can express Bob's operation on $\\mathsf{B}$ like this:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_{\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{-\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  Seperti yang kita lakukan untuk Alice, kita bisa mengekspresikan operasi Bob pada $\\mathsf{B}$ seperti ini:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_{\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{-\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  After Bob applies this operation, he measures $\\mathsf{B}$ with a "
"standard basis measurement and sets his answer $b$ to be the measurement "
"outcome.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Setelah Bob menerapkan operasi ini, dia mengukur $\\mathsf{B}$ dengan "
"pengukuran basis standar dan menetapkan jawabannya $b$ sebagai hasil "
"pengukuran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here is a quantum circuit diagram that describes this strategy:\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah diagram Circuit kuantum yang mendeskripsikan strategi ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![CHSH game circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/CHSH.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![CHSH game circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/CHSH.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this diagram we see two ordinary controlled gates, one for $U_{-\\pi/8}$ on the top and one for $U_{\\pi/4}$ on the bottom.\n"
"We also have two gates that look like controlled gates, one for $U_{\\pi/8}$ on the top and one for $U_{0}$ on the bottom, except that the circle representing the control is not filled in.\n"
"This denotes a different type of controlled gate where the gate is performed if the control is set to $0$ (rather than $1$ like an ordinary controlled gate).\n"
"So, effectively, Bob performs $U_{\\pi/8}$ on his qubit if $y=0$ and $U_{-\\pi/8}$ if $y=1;$\n"
"and Alice performs $U_0$ on her qubit if $x=0$ and $U_{\\pi/4}$ if $x=1,$ which is consistent with the description of the protocol in words above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam diagram ini kita melihat dua Gate terkontrol biasa, satu untuk $U_{-\\pi/8}$ di atas dan satu untuk $U_{\\pi/4}$ di bawah.\n"
"Kita juga memiliki dua Gate yang terlihat seperti Gate terkontrol, satu untuk $U_{\\pi/8}$ di atas dan satu untuk $U_{0}$ di bawah, kecuali bahwa lingkaran yang mewakili kontrol tidak terisi.\n"
"Ini menandakan jenis Gate terkontrol yang berbeda di mana Gate dilakukan jika kontrol diatur ke $0$ (bukan $1$ seperti Gate terkontrol biasa).\n"
"Jadi, secara efektif, Bob melakukan $U_{\\pi/8}$ pada Qubitnya jika $y=0$ dan $U_{-\\pi/8}$ jika $y=1;$\n"
"dan Alice melakukan $U_0$ pada Qubitnya jika $x=0$ dan $U_{\\pi/4}$ jika $x=1,$ yang konsisten dengan deskripsi protokol dalam kata-kata di atas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It remains to figure out how well this strategy for Alice and Bob works.\n"
"We'll do this by going through the four possible question pairs individually.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masih perlu dipahami seberapa baik strategi ini bekerja untuk Alice dan Bob.\n"
"Kita akan melakukan ini dengan melalui empat pasangan pertanyaan yang mungkin satu per satu.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Case-by-case analysis {#case-by-case-analysis}"
msgstr "Analisis kasus per kasus {#case-by-case-analysis}"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Case 1:  $(x,y) = (0,0).$\n"
msgstr "Kasus 1: $(x,y) = (0,0).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In this case Alice performs $U_{0}$ on her qubit and Bob performs "
"$U_{\\pi/8}$ on his, so the state of the two qubits "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ after they perform their operations is\n"
msgstr ""
"   Dalam kasus ini Alice melakukan $U_{0}$ pada Qubitnya dan Bob melakukan "
"$U_{\\pi/8}$ pada miliknya, sehingga keadaan dua qubit "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ setelah mereka melakukan operasinya adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_0 \\otimes U_{\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_0 \\otimes U_{\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The probabilities for the four possible answer pairs $(a,b)$ are "
"therefore as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Probabilitas untuk empat kemungkinan pasangan jawaban $(a,b)$ adalah "
"sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   We can then obtain the probabilities that $a=b$ and $a\\neq b$ by "
"summing.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Kita kemudian bisa mendapatkan probabilitas bahwa $a=b$ dan $a\\neq b$ "
"dengan menjumlahkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   For the question pair $(0,0),$ Alice and Bob win if $a=b,$ and therefore "
"they win in this case with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"   Untuk pasangan pertanyaan $(0,0),$ Alice dan Bob menang jika $a=b,$ "
"sehingga mereka menang dalam kasus ini dengan probabilitas\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Case 2:  $(x,y) = (0,1).$\n"
msgstr "Kasus 2: $(x,y) = (0,1).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In this case Alice performs $U_{0}$ on her qubit and Bob performs "
"$U_{-\\pi/8}$ on his, so the state of the two qubits "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ after they perform their operations is\n"
msgstr ""
"   Dalam kasus ini Alice melakukan $U_{0}$ pada Qubitnya dan Bob melakukan "
"$U_{-\\pi/8}$ pada miliknya, sehingga keadaan dua qubit "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ setelah mereka melakukan operasinya adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_0 \\otimes U_{-\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_0 \\otimes U_{-\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Again, we can obtain the probabilities that $a=b$ and $a\\neq b$ by "
"summing.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Sekali lagi, kita bisa mendapatkan probabilitas bahwa $a=b$ dan $a\\neq "
"b$ dengan menjumlahkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   For the question pair $(0,1),$ Alice and Bob win if $a=b,$ and therefore "
"they win in this case with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"   Untuk pasangan pertanyaan $(0,1),$ Alice dan Bob menang jika $a=b,$ "
"sehingga mereka menang dalam kasus ini dengan probabilitas\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Case 3:  $(x,y) = (1,0).$\n"
msgstr "Kasus 3: $(x,y) = (1,0).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In this case Alice performs $U_{\\pi/4}$ on her qubit and Bob performs "
"$U_{\\pi/8}$ on his, so the state of the two qubits "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ after they perform their operations is\n"
msgstr ""
"   Dalam kasus ini Alice melakukan $U_{\\pi/4}$ pada Qubitnya dan Bob "
"melakukan $U_{\\pi/8}$ pada miliknya, sehingga keadaan dua qubit "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ setelah mereka melakukan operasinya adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_{\\pi/4} \\otimes U_{\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_{\\pi/4} \\otimes U_{\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   We find, once again, that probabilities that $a=b$ and $a\\neq b$ are as "
"follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Kita menemukan, sekali lagi, bahwa probabilitas bahwa $a=b$ dan $a\\neq "
"b$ adalah sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   For the question pair $(1,0),$ Alice and Bob win if $a=b,$ so they win in"
" this case with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"   Untuk pasangan pertanyaan $(1,0),$ Alice dan Bob menang jika $a=b,$ jadi "
"mereka menang dalam kasus ini dengan probabilitas\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Case 4:  $(x,y) = (1,1).$\n"
msgstr "Kasus 4: $(x,y) = (1,1).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The last case is a little bit different, as we might expect because the "
"winning condition is different in this case. When $x$ and $y$ are both $1,$ "
"Alice and Bob win when $a$ and $b$ are *different*. In this case Alice "
"performs $U_{\\pi/4}$ on her qubit and Bob performs $U_{-\\pi/8}$ on his, so"
" the state of the two qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ after they perform "
"their operations is\n"
msgstr ""
"   Kasus terakhir sedikit berbeda, seperti yang mungkin kita harapkan karena"
" kondisi menang berbeda dalam kasus ini. Ketika $x$ dan $y$ keduanya $1,$ "
"Alice dan Bob menang ketika $a$ dan $b$ *berbeda*. Dalam kasus ini Alice "
"melakukan $U_{\\pi/4}$ pada Qubitnya dan Bob melakukan $U_{-\\pi/8}$ pada "
"miliknya, sehingga keadaan dua qubit $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ setelah "
"mereka melakukan operasinya adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_{\\pi/4} \\otimes U_{-\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_{\\pi/4} \\otimes U_{-\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The probabilities have effectively swapped places from in the three other cases.\n"
"   We obtain the probabilities that $a=b$ and $a\\neq b$ by summing.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Probabilitas-probabilitas secara efektif bertukar tempat dari tiga kasus lainnya.\n"
"   Kita mendapatkan probabilitas bahwa $a=b$ dan $a\\neq b$ dengan menjumlahkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   For the question pair $(1,1),$ Alice and Bob win if $a\\neq b,$ and "
"therefore they win in this case with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"   Untuk pasangan pertanyaan $(1,1),$ Alice dan Bob menang jika $a\\neq b,$ "
"sehingga mereka menang dalam kasus ini dengan probabilitas\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "They win in every case with the same probability:\n"
msgstr "Mereka menang di setiap kasus dengan probabilitas yang sama:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} \\approx 0.85.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} \\approx 0.85.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is therefore the probability that they win overall.\n"
"That's significantly better than any classical strategy can do for this game; classical strategies have winning probability bounded by $3/4.$ And that makes this a very interesting example.\n"
msgstr ""
"Inilah probabilitas mereka menang secara keseluruhan.\n"
"Itu jauh lebih baik dari strategi klasik mana pun yang bisa dilakukan untuk permainan ini; strategi klasik memiliki probabilitas menang yang dibatasi oleh $3/4.$ Dan itu menjadikan ini contoh yang sangat menarik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This happens to be the *optimal* winning probability for quantum strategies; we can't do any better than this, no matter what entangled state or measurements we choose.\n"
"This fact is known as *Tsirelson's inequality*, named for Boris Tsirelson who first proved it — and who first described the CHSH experiment as a game.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini kebetulan merupakan probabilitas menang *optimal* untuk strategi kuantum; kita tidak bisa berbuat lebih baik dari ini, tidak peduli keadaan terikat atau pengukuran apa yang kita pilih.\n"
"Fakta ini dikenal sebagai *ketidaksetaraan Tsirelson*, dinamai berdasarkan Boris Tsirelson yang pertama kali membuktikannya — dan yang pertama kali mendeskripsikan eksperimen CHSH sebagai permainan.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Geometric picture {#geometric-picture}"
msgstr "Gambaran geometris {#geometric-picture}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is possible to think about the strategy described above geometrically, "
"which may be helpful for understanding the relationships among the various "
"angles chosen for Alice and Bob's operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dimungkinkan untuk memikirkan strategi yang dijelaskan di atas secara "
"geometris, yang mungkin berguna untuk memahami hubungan antar berbagai sudut"
" yang dipilih untuk operasi Alice dan Bob.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What Alice effectively does is to choose an angle $\\alpha,$ depending on her question $x,$ and then to apply $U_{\\alpha}$ to her qubit and measure.\n"
"Similarly, Bob chooses an angle $\\beta,$ depending on $y,$ and then he applies $U_{\\beta}$ to his qubit and measures.\n"
"We've chosen $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Yang secara efektif Alice lakukan adalah memilih sudut $\\alpha,$ bergantung pada pertanyaannya $x,$ kemudian menerapkan $U_{\\alpha}$ pada Qubitnya dan mengukur.\n"
"Demikian pula, Bob memilih sudut $\\beta,$ bergantung pada $y,$ kemudian dia menerapkan $U_{\\beta}$ pada Qubitnya dan mengukur.\n"
"Kita telah memilih $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$ sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\alpha & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"0 & x=0\\\\\n"
"\\pi/4 & x=1\n"
"\\end{cases}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\beta & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\pi/8 & y = 0\\\\\n"
"-\\pi/8 & y = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\alpha & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"0 & x=0\\\\\n"
"\\pi/4 & x=1\n"
"\\end{cases}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\beta & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\pi/8 & y = 0\\\\\n"
"-\\pi/8 & y = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the moment, though, let's take $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ to be arbitrary.\n"
"By choosing $\\alpha,$ Alice effectively defines an orthonormal basis of vectors that looks like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk sementara, mari kita ambil $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$ sebagai sembarang.\n"
"Dengan memilih $\\alpha,$ Alice secara efektif mendefinisikan basis ortonormal dari vektor yang terlihat seperti ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Basis for Alice](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/alpha-basis.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Basis for Alice](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/alpha-basis.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bob does likewise, except that his angle is $\\beta$:\n"
msgstr "Bob juga melakukan hal yang sama, kecuali sudutnya adalah $\\beta$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Basis for Bob](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/beta-basis.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Basis for Bob](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/beta-basis.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The colors of the vectors correspond to Alice and Bob's answers: blue for "
"$0$ and red for $1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Warna vektor-vektor tersebut sesuai dengan jawaban Alice dan Bob: biru untuk"
" $0$ dan merah untuk $1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now, if we combine together ($3$) and ($4$) we get the formula\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, jika kita menggabungkan ($3$) dan ($4$) kita mendapatkan rumus\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle;\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle;\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "this works for all real numbers $\\alpha$ and $\\beta.$\n"
msgstr "ini berlaku untuk semua bilangan real $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Following the same sort of analysis that we went through above, but with "
"$\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ being variables, we find this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan mengikuti jenis analisis yang sama seperti yang kita lakukan di atas,"
" tetapi dengan $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$ sebagai variabel, kita menemukan "
"ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  & \\bigl(U_{\\alpha} \\otimes U_{\\beta}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad =\n"
"    \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta + \\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\frac{\n"
"        \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 11\\rangle\n"
"      }{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  & \\bigl(U_{\\alpha} \\otimes U_{\\beta}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad =\n"
"    \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta + \\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\frac{\n"
"        \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 11\\rangle\n"
"      }{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We conclude these two formulas:\n"
msgstr "Kita menyimpulkan dua rumus ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a = b)  & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\cos^2(\\alpha - \\beta)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\sin^2(\\alpha - \\beta).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a = b)  & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\cos^2(\\alpha - \\beta)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\sin^2(\\alpha - \\beta).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These equations can be connected to the figures above by imagining that we "
"superimpose the bases chosen by Alice and Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Persamaan-persamaan ini bisa dihubungkan dengan gambar-gambar di atas dengan"
" membayangkan kita menumpangkan basis yang dipilih oleh Alice dan Bob.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Explore the strategy {#explore-the-strategy}"
msgstr "Jelajahi strategi {#explore-the-strategy}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When $(x,y) = (0,0),$ Alice and Bob choose $\\alpha = 0$ and $\\beta = "
"\\pi/8,$ and by superimposing their bases we obtain this figure:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ketika $(x,y) = (0,0),$ Alice dan Bob memilih $\\alpha = 0$ dan $\\beta = "
"\\pi/8,$ dan dengan menumpangkan basis mereka kita mendapatkan gambar ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/strategy00.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/strategy00.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The angle between the red vectors is $\\pi/8,$ which is the same as the angle between the two blue vectors.\n"
"The probability that Alice and Bob's outcomes agree is the cosine-squared of this angle,\n"
msgstr ""
"Sudut antara vektor-vektor merah adalah $\\pi/8,$ yang sama dengan sudut antara dua vektor biru.\n"
"Probabilitas hasil Alice dan Bob sama adalah kuadrat cosinus dari sudut ini,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "while the probability they disagree is the sine-squared of this angle,\n"
msgstr ""
"sementara probabilitas mereka tidak sama adalah kuadrat sinus dari sudut "
"ini,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sin^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sin^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When $(x,y) = (0,1),$ Alice and Bob choose $\\alpha = 0$ and $\\beta = "
"-\\pi/8,$ and by superimposing their bases we obtain this figure:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ketika $(x,y) = (0,1),$ Alice dan Bob memilih $\\alpha = 0$ dan $\\beta = "
"-\\pi/8,$ dan dengan menumpangkan basis mereka kita mendapatkan gambar "
"ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/strategy01.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/strategy01.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The angle between the red vectors is again $\\pi/8,$ as is the angle between the blue vectors.\n"
"The probability that Alice and Bob's outcomes agree is again the cosine-squared of this angle,\n"
msgstr ""
"Sudut antara vektor-vektor merah lagi-lagi $\\pi/8,$ begitu pula sudut antara vektor-vektor biru.\n"
"Probabilitas hasil Alice dan Bob sama lagi-lagi adalah kuadrat cosinus dari sudut ini,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When $(x,y) = (1,0),$ Alice and Bob choose $\\alpha = \\pi/4$ and $\\beta = "
"\\pi/8,$ and by superimposing their bases we obtain this figure:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ketika $(x,y) = (1,0),$ Alice dan Bob memilih $\\alpha = \\pi/4$ dan $\\beta"
" = \\pi/8,$ dan dengan menumpangkan basis mereka kita mendapatkan gambar "
"ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/strategy10.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/strategy10.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bases have changed but the angles haven't — once again the angle between vectors of the same color is $\\pi/8.$\n"
"The probability that Alice and Bob's outcomes agree is\n"
msgstr ""
"Basisnya telah berubah tetapi sudut-sudutnya belum — sekali lagi sudut antara vektor-vektor dengan warna yang sama adalah $\\pi/8.$\n"
"Probabilitas hasil Alice dan Bob sama adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and the probability they disagree is\n"
msgstr "dan probabilitas mereka tidak sama adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When $(x,y) = (1,1),$ Alice and Bob choose $\\alpha = \\pi/4$ and $\\beta = "
"-\\pi/8.$ When we superimpose their bases, we see that something different "
"has happened:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ketika $(x,y) = (1,1),$ Alice dan Bob memilih $\\alpha = \\pi/4$ dan $\\beta"
" = -\\pi/8.$ Ketika kita menumpangkan basis mereka, kita melihat sesuatu "
"yang berbeda telah terjadi:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/strategy11.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/strategy11.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By the way the angles were chosen, this time the angle between vectors having the same color is $3\\pi/8$ rather than $\\pi/8.$\n"
"The probability that Alice and Bob's outcomes agree is still the cosine-squared of this angle, but this time the value is\n"
msgstr ""
"Berdasarkan cara sudut-sudut dipilih, kali ini sudut antara vektor-vektor yang memiliki warna sama adalah $3\\pi/8$ bukan $\\pi/8.$\n"
"Probabilitas hasil Alice dan Bob sama masih kuadrat cosinus dari sudut ini, tetapi kali ini nilainya adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The probability the outcomes disagree is the sine-squared of this angle, "
"which in this case is this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Probabilitas hasil tidak sama adalah kuadrat sinus dari sudut ini, yang "
"dalam kasus ini adalah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sin^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sin^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Remarks {#remarks}"
msgstr "Catatan {#remarks}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The basic idea of an experiment like the CHSH game, where entanglement leads to statistical results that are inconsistent with purely classical reasoning, is due to John Bell, the namesake of the Bell states.\n"
"For this reason, people often refer to experiments of this sort as *Bell tests*.\n"
"Sometimes people also refer to *Bell's theorem*, which can be formulated in different ways — but the essence of it is that quantum mechanics is not compatible with so-called *local hidden variable theories*.\n"
"The CHSH game is a particularly clean and simple example of a Bell test, and can be viewed as a proof, or demonstration, of Bell's theorem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ide dasar dari eksperimen seperti permainan CHSH, di mana keterikatan menghasilkan hasil statistik yang tidak konsisten dengan penalaran murni klasik, adalah karya John Bell, pemberi nama dari keadaan Bell.\n"
"Karena alasan inilah, orang-orang sering menyebut eksperimen semacam ini sebagai *uji Bell*.\n"
"Terkadang orang juga menyebut *teorema Bell*, yang bisa dirumuskan dalam berbagai cara — tetapi intinya adalah bahwa mekanika kuantum tidak kompatibel dengan yang disebut *teori variabel tersembunyi lokal*.\n"
"Permainan CHSH adalah contoh uji Bell yang sangat bersih dan sederhana, dan bisa dipandang sebagai bukti, atau demonstrasi, dari teorema Bell.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The CHSH game offers a way to experimentally test the theory of quantum information.\n"
"We can perform experiments that implement the CHSH game, and test the sorts of strategies based on entanglement described above.\n"
"This provides us with a high degree of confidence that entanglement is real — and unlike the sometimes vague or poetic ways that we come up with to explain entanglement, the CHSH game gives us a concrete and testable way to *observe* entanglement.\n"
"The 2022 Nobel Prize in Physics acknowledges the importance of this line of work: the prize was awarded to Alain Aspect, John Clauser (the C in CHSH), and Anton Zeilinger, for observing entanglement through Bell tests on entangled photons.\n"
msgstr ""
"Permainan CHSH menawarkan cara untuk menguji teori informasi kuantum secara eksperimental.\n"
"Kita bisa melakukan eksperimen yang mengimplementasikan permainan CHSH, dan menguji jenis strategi berdasarkan keterikatan yang dijelaskan di atas.\n"
"Ini memberi kita tingkat kepercayaan yang tinggi bahwa keterikatan itu nyata — dan tidak seperti cara-cara yang terkadang samar atau puitis yang kita gunakan untuk menjelaskan keterikatan, permainan CHSH memberi kita cara yang konkret dan dapat diuji untuk *mengamati* keterikatan.\n"
"Hadiah Nobel Fisika 2022 mengakui pentingnya garis penelitian ini: hadiah diberikan kepada Alain Aspect, John Clauser (C dalam CHSH), dan Anton Zeilinger, karena mengamati keterikatan melalui uji Bell pada foton yang terikat.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit implementation {#qiskit-implementation}"
msgstr "Implementasi Qiskit {#qiskit-implementation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can implement the CHSH game, together with the quantum strategy defined "
"above, in Qiskit as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita bisa mengimplementasikan permainan CHSH, beserta strategi kuantum yang "
"didefinisikan di atas, dalam Qiskit sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, here's the definition of the game itself, which allows an arbitrary "
"strategy to be plugged in as an argument.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, berikut adalah definisi permainan itu sendiri, yang memungkinkan "
"strategi sembarang dimasukkan sebagai argumen.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we'll create a function that outputs a circuit depending on the "
"questions for Alice and Bob. We'll let the qubits have their default names "
"for simplicity, and we'll use the built-in $R_y(\\theta)$ gate for Alice and"
" Bob's actions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita akan membuat fungsi yang menghasilkan Circuit tergantung pada "
"pertanyaan untuk Alice dan Bob. Kita akan membiarkan qubit memiliki nama "
"default mereka untuk kesederhanaan, dan kita akan menggunakan Gate "
"$R_y(\\theta)$ bawaan untuk tindakan Alice dan Bob.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here are the four possible circuits, depending on which questions are "
"asked.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah empat kemungkinan Circuit, tergantung pertanyaan mana yang "
"diajukan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/extracted-"
"outputs/4f57a9c8-1.avif)\n"
